+## Read next when creating a new part
+
+A new part touches four other areas. Read these before writing code, and skip the rest of `references/`:
+- `skills/tessel-frontend/references/localization.md` — where string files live and how keys are named.
+- `skills/tessel-frontend/references/state-and-data.md` — persisted UI state (e.g. dismissals) and which store to use.
+- `skills/tessel-frontend/references/testing.md` — the spec file, `renderPart`, and how to drive interactions.
+- `skills/tessel-frontend/references/git-pr-ci-release.md` — the change note every user-visible change needs.
